<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karim ul-Makhdum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Sheikh Karimal Makdum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karim ul-Makhdum was an Arab or Persian Muslim missionary who, according to Sulu tradition, arrived in the Sulu archipelago in the late fourteenth century, traditionally in 1380, and helped spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> there. He is credited with founding the mosque at Tubig Indangan on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simunul">Simunul</a> island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tawi-tawi">Tawi-Tawi</a>, regarded as the oldest mosque in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p></div>
